292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (Sir Fazle Hasan Abed was born on April 27, 1936, in Baniachong, a remote village in northeastern Bangladesh \(then British India\). He came from a distinguished family- his maternal grandfather served as ministers for agriculture and education in Bengal during the final years of British Colonial rule. Despite his priviledged background as a zamindar \(Landowner\) family member, Abed showed an early inclination toward social consciousness. He completed his secondary education at Pabna Zilla School and intermediate studies at Dhaka College. At age 18, he left home to oursue naval architecture at the University of Glasgow in Scotland, later qualifying as a Cost Management Accountant in London. This technical education provided him with the analytical rigor and financial acumen that would later distinguish his approach to development work- combining the precision of accounting with the compassion of humanitarian concern. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
