/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (What distinguishes BRAC from traditional NGOs is its holistic ecosystem approach. Rather than remaining a single-purpose organization, BRAC intentionally diversified into interconnected programs and social enterprises. The organization comprises development programs, microfinance operations, social enterprises including BRAC Bank, BRAC University, and various for-profit ventures, and mission-aligned investments. This unique structure reflects Abed's conviction that poverty alleviation requires multi-dimensional, integrated solutions. Programs in microfinance are paired with business training; education initiatives are linked with livelihood development; health services connect to nutrition and sanitation programs. This integration of development and business approaches became Abed's signature strategy for sustainable impact.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
