/P 164 0 R
/T ( Ethical Leadership and Moral Conviction)
/E ( Ethical Leadership and Moral Conviction)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (Abed's leadership was fundamentally rooted in ethical principles. He refused to compromise BRAC's independence or mission, even when faced with political pressure. In one notable instance, politicians approached him asking him to use BRAC's influence to affect voting behavior of his employees. Abed refused categorically, stating that BRAC was apolitical and existed to serve the poor, not political interests. This commitment to ethical boundaries helped BRAC maintain credibility and independence throughout decades of political instability in Bangladesh. His famous quote- "I have met many defeated men in my life. I have never met a defeated woman" which reflects his core conviction that human dignity, potential, and agency are universal and not determined by circumstance. This ethical )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
