/E (Abed communicated through both formal and informal channels. He regularly wrote thought pieces and gave interviews explaining BRAC's vision and approach. His communication was marked by clarity, intellectual humility and strategic framing. Rather than relying on inspirational rhetoric, he communicated through stories, evidence, and logic. He was known for listening deeply to field staff and incorporating their insights into organizational strategy. This communication style created genuine engagement rather than mere compliance, allowing BRAC to function as a learning organization even as it scaled. His repeated phrases like "Small is beautiful, scale is necessary" and emphasis on "blending business acumen with development practice" became part of BRAC's organizational language, shaping how staff understood their roles and decisions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
