/P 166 0 R
/E (Abed understood that BRAC's success ultimately depended on the motivation and capability of its staff. He created an organizational culture where employees felt they were part of a historic mission. Staff were recruited not primarily for technical skills but for commitment to the mission with technical training  provided  on the  job. BRAC  offered  modest  salaries  compared  to  corporate  positions, yet )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
