/P 167 0 R
/E (attracted and retained talented people because the work was meaningful. Abed fostered an environment of intellectual engagement where staff were expected to think critically, question approaches, and contribute ideas. The organization invested heavily in staff development and learning. Despite BRAC's size, Abed maintained accessibility to leadership, creating psychological safety for dissenting views. This institutional culture proved crucial for sustaining quality as BRAC expanded internationally. The organization faced challenges when operating in new countries, but its strong organizational culture and commitment to learning allowed it to adapt while maintaining core principles)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
