341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (In the context of Bangladesh, where corruption was endemic, Abed's unwavering commitment to organizational integrity was remarkable and consequential. BRAC developed robust systems for financial accountability and transparency which were essential for maintaining donor confidence and staff motivation. Abed refused to engage in political patronage or compromise organizational principles for short-term gains. This integrity built BRAC's reputation, making it a trusted partner for governments, international organizations, and donors. More profoundly, the ethical culture permeated all levels of the organization. Staff understood that cutting corners or compromising quality was not acceptable, regardless of external pressure. This commitment to quality and integrity became embedded in BRAC's brand, helping it attract resources and partnerships.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 167 0 R
/T ( Financial Discipline)
/E ( Financial Discipline)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (Abed's background as a management accountant directly shaped his approach to financial management. BRAC maintained rigorous financial controls, transparent accounting, and rigorous cost-effectiveness analysis of all programs. Every major initiative was subjected to financial scrutiny: What was the cost per beneficiary? How could the same impact be achieved at lower cost? Could the program eventually become self-financing? This financial discipline prevented the bloat and inefficiency that sometimes affects large development organizations. It also enabled BRAC to optimize resource allocation, directing funds to activities with the highest impact. Abed's insistence on cost-effectiveness didn't mean cutting corners on quality; rather, it meant identifying the most efficient way to deliver quality. This balance of excellence with efficiency became BRAC's operational hallmark and a key reason for its impact per dollar spent.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
