/P 170 0 R
/E (BRAC's expansion beyond Bangladesh in 2002 brought new challenges. Operating in different countries with distinct legal, cultural, and institutional contexts required significant adaptation. Early international programs faced implementation challenges, with some initiatives requiring course corrections. The question of whether BRAC's Bangladesh-tested models could be successfully transplanted to other contexts proved more complex than anticipated. This highlighted that Abed's leadership, while creating strong institutional culture, was also intensely personalized. Questions about succession and institutional continuity loomed as Abed aged. How would BRAC maintain its mission and culture without its founder's active guidance? This concern became acute following Abed's death in December 2019, leaving BRAC to navigate institutional transformation.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
